      "ending": "All selected exponent columns eventually lie in one fixed compact subset of the original P interior. Original graded full-density saturation, read through its proof ending, includes them for every sufficiently large integer k. This uses the original graded semigroup, not a fictitiously graded assembled union. Flag transfer then gives the mixed section minor. Surjectivity on constant quotients excludes collisions. For a fixed real vector this is a direct degreewise construction. Nonempty open rank loci and a countable intersection over k give a very-general tuple. At fixed length, countably many rational strict vectors and rational parameters provide a common locus; approximate real vectors from below and close the nef cone. This does not assert boundary jet surjectivity from closedness of rank.",
